      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Brussels, the palace of entrenched power, is preparing its final sentence. Under competition law, the targeted conglomerate Alphabet faces a financial shakedown for alleged anti-competitive ranking of its units. The regulatory agencies have rejected the company's remedy proposals, and a decision is pending. This monetary sanction is just the latest in a long history of fines, a state-sanctioned theft disguised as market regulation.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "why-1",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
