      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.75
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "For two years, Google has been the system's scapegoat, besieged by government regulators enforcing a corrupt order. The European authorities prepare a crushing blow—a massive antitrust fine—for the alleged anti-competitive ranking that favored its own services over market competitors. This penalty, expected soon, adds to a decade of accumulated fines, a pattern of the state financially targeting a multinational corporation it deems too powerful.",
